{
  "task": "summarize",
  "input": "Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA) is an architectural style in software engineering where services provide functionality to other components via a communication protocol over a network. An API Gateway is a server that acts as an API front-end, receives API requests, enforces throttling and security policies, passes requests to the backend service, and passes the response back to the requester. In microservice architectures, the gateway insulates clients from microservice partitioning."
}

