  "task": "explain",
  "input": "Kubernetes Pods are the smallest deployable units of computing that you can create and manage in Kubernetes. A Pod is a group of one or more containers, with shared storage and network resources, and a specification for how to run the containers."
}

{
  "task": "key_points",
  "input": "Prometheus is an open-source systems monitoring and alerting toolkit. It collects and stores metrics as time series data, where metrics information is stored with the timestamp at which it was recorded, alongside optional key-value pairs called labels. Prometheus relies on a pull model over HTTP."
}

